      "side": 1,
      "message": "I couldn’t find a separate prose style guide for this rule.\nThe project’s formatting configuration is in .clang-format(https://github.com/openbmc/entity-manager/blob/master/.clang-format).\n\nColumnLimit: 80 is present in the repository from its 2018 import (https://github.com/openbmc/entity-manager/commit/3cb5fece5e1c0ed68ac26766ca2ae7c4a8996be4).\n\nBreakStringLiterals: false was added in 2023 (https://github.com/openbmc/entity-manager/commit/df19061984becd834fdb324a41ae262920e73bbf). \nBoth predate clang-format 23.1.6, so this is not a new restriction introduced by that version.",
      "parentUuid": "31f5e889_876f7f34",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 8,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 9,
