      "writtenOn": "2026-11-17T07:29:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Understood. \nI’ll keep long string literals intact for searchability rather than split them just to meet the column limit. \nWith this project configuration, clang-format 23.1.6 preserves the long literal and wraps the surrounding call instead.\n\nhttps://github.com/openbmc/entity-manager/blob/master/.clang-format\n\nThe relevant settings are BreakStringLiterals: false and ColumnLimit: 80; the corresponding options are documented in the clang-format style options\n(https://clang.llvm.org/docs/ClangFormatStyleOptions.html#breakstringliterals)",
      "parentUuid": "e88685ae_a43844a1",
      "revId": "e0b917a4b8a8ebe68cae1d2cac5511803c4c4c60",
